{
  "slug": "gangsta",
  "name": "Gangsta",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "AI agentic skills framework for spec-driven development — mafia-syndicate hierarchy with adversarial brainstorming, institutional memory, and governance guardrails",
  "longDescription": "Ships **19 skills**, **6 agents** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (19): `audit-review` (Use when completing tasks, implementing major features, or before merging — dispatches the-inspector to audit the books before…), `drill-tdd` (Use when implementing any feature or bugfix — enforces the Red-Green-Refactor drill with no production code allowed without…), `exit-strategy` (Use when implementation is complete and all tests pass — guides the clean exit from a development branch…), `interrogation-debugging` (Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior — finds the rat in the code through…), `laundering` (Use when all territories report completion after the hit — handles integration, verification, consigliere final review, cleanup, and…), `omerta` (Use when enforcing governance guardrails during any gangsta operation — referenced as cross-cutting concern by all skills for…), `receiving-orders` (Use when receiving code review feedback — processes orders with technical rigor, not blind obedience or performative agreement), `reconnaissance` (Use when beginning a new heist — deploys associates to survey the target codebase, existing tests, dependencies, documentation,…), and 11 more\n- **Agents** (6): `associate` (Use this agent for specialized external tasks — codebase scanning, dependency audits, documentation retrieval, API integration, and other…), `devils-advocate` (Use this agent during The Grilling (single-pass) to attack the proposed solution), `proposer` (Use this agent during The Grilling to propose architectural solutions based on the reconnaissance dossier), `soldier` (Use this agent for stateless code execution — implementing a single work package with TDD enforcement), `synthesizer` (Use this agent during The Grilling to mediate between proposer and devils-advocate), `the-inspector` (Use this agent for independent code inspection — reviews git diffs against requirements, categorizes issues by severity, and…)\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install gangsta@claude-community` from `kucherenko/gangsta`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 19,
    "agent": 6,
    "hook": 1
  },
